But it also increases hit points, and your chance of surviving
an encounter with the monster.

> - and
> descending a dungeon level means more equipment to find.
> Lingering on explored levels is somewhere between pointless
> (with a combat class) and counterproductive.

Linger too long, and you'll have problems with hunger.  Go down
too fast, and the monsters will be too tough for you.  If there
were a simple, definitive answer, it wouldn't be Nethack.

In general, however, I wouldn't leave a level (at least for
about the first 10 levels) until it had been completely
explored.  And generally, I don't like going much deeper than my
experience level.  But those are just generalities.  Exceptional
situations (like finding +3 plate mail on the first level) will
lead to exceptions, and I've also reached minetown with XP
1 (once, in a game in which I ascended).

